  "reason": "The change restructures provider tool-history replay: the turn ledger checkpoint advances in blocks and rides with the last operator message instead of the instructions, failed/denied steps fold with failure facts, ToolCall intents and tool.proposed events reference the ledger intent row instead of copying reasoning, ledger rows of one step share replay state, the unread checkpoint_through_step write is dropped, and Chat Completions cache hits are recorded. Selected: the new prompt-cache/ledger regression file; the ledger throughput and in-turn pruning files; the chat tool loop, tool failure and turn outcome files; provider adapters (usage parsing); reasoning replay; the test_chat.py restart/recovery/tool nodes that read provider_history_intent and replay; the passing subagent round/restart nodes; and the context-length rejection recovery node.",
  "exclusions": "Full suites are not approved and are excluded. Node-level selections leave out tests that already fail on pristine origin/main 4facf4a in this environment (16 functions in tests/v3/test_chat.py, 14 in tests/v3/test_chat_subagents.py, tests/v3/test_reasoning_replay.py::test_a_step_core_delivers_is_a_batch_of_its_own, and the test_chat_leftovers routing-commentary case; identical failure sets with and without this change, owned by the resume-admission and other audit PRs). No UI, Playwright, native Rust/Tauri, harness, mission or migration code changes: ChatTokenUsage gains a defaulted field inside existing JSON payloads and no table changes. A scratch real-Core OpenRouter run is recorded in the PR body.",
